[{:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-93685"] :question/problem "$$\n[\\begin{aligned}a & 0 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & b \\\\ 0 & 0 & c\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe matrix of the bilinear form $B(x,y)={x}_{1}{y}_{1}-3{x}_{1}{y}_{3}+{x}_{2}{y}_{3}-{x}_{3}{y}_{3}$ is given above. What is the value of $a+b+c?$" :question/worked-solution "Each term ${a}_{ij}{x}_{i}{y}_{j}$ in the expression of the bilinear form corresponds to the entry ${a}_{ij}$ of the matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B(x,y) & ={x}_{1}{y}_{1}-3{x}_{1}{y}_{3}+{x}_{2}{y}_{3}-{x}_{3}{y}_{3} \\\\  & =1{x}_{1}{y}_{1}+0{x}_{1}{y}_{2}+(-3){x}_{1}{y}_{3} \\\\  & +\\,0{x}_{2}{y}_{1}+0{x}_{2}{y}_{2}+1{x}_{2}{y}_{3} \\\\  & +\\,0{x}_{3}{y}_{1}+0{x}_{3}{y}_{2}+(-1){x}_{3}{y}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, the corresponding matrix of the bilinear form is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=1,$ $b=1,$ and $c=-1.$ Finally, \n\n$$\na+b+c=1+1+(-1)=1.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-93982/selection/82223557124b132584b16ae46cc4c4a030e1098c3904b38b1d55f32853923cb3" :answer/id #uuid "b514cf9c-3dc3-565f-9ff6-2cf8a817bff8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2{x}_{1}{y}_{1}+{x}_{1}{y}_{2}-{x}_{2}{y}_{1}+3{x}_{2}{y}_{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-93982/selection/9eeac355f10c1e3bbebb01e8f2a78c3ee0ac3da7731a6b6a15c8a8951d651ae5" :answer/id #uuid "131a7aaa-60e1-5667-89b9-05264d0c1f9c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3{x}_{1}{y}_{1}+{x}_{1}{y}_{2}+{x}_{2}{y}_{1}+2{x}_{2}{y}_{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-93982/selection/c48ad081769da8e6bc1c5c16a030598da8229f58dea0cf5670da6abbf84166e5" :answer/id #uuid "7d6b4b41-bce9-59b2-a5c5-e7b971b3c199" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2{x}_{1}{y}_{1}+{x}_{1}{y}_{2}-3{x}_{2}{y}_{1}+2{x}_{2}{y}_{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-93982/selection/229e15b5ca20cc34434923f52fd5f795b715c0ec7b83ed5fda22c154fff4f43a" :answer/id #uuid "817a6e53-bae3-5084-b075-af5376788550" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2{x}_{1}{y}_{1}-{x}_{1}{y}_{2}-{x}_{2}{y}_{1}+{x}_{2}{y}_{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-93982/selection/d329eb2cfe1e45b202a882b919adbe3a30dcd36b8ae052be410fce81fb55ae78" :answer/id #uuid "e735d04e-5ce8-5cdb-bba8-d247ff2be594" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3{x}_{1}{y}_{1}+{x}_{1}{y}_{2}-{x}_{2}{y}_{1}+2{x}_{2}{y}_{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-93982/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "130441bc-66e3-5d38-9a11-87ef6ff299d7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-93982/selection/d329eb2cfe1e45b202a882b919adbe3a30dcd36b8ae052be410fce81fb55ae78" :answer-field/choices ["q-93982/selection/82223557124b132584b16ae46cc4c4a030e1098c3904b38b1d55f32853923cb3" "q-93982/selection/9eeac355f10c1e3bbebb01e8f2a78c3ee0ac3da7731a6b6a15c8a8951d651ae5" "q-93982/selection/c48ad081769da8e6bc1c5c16a030598da8229f58dea0cf5670da6abbf84166e5" "q-93982/selection/229e15b5ca20cc34434923f52fd5f795b715c0ec7b83ed5fda22c154fff4f43a" "q-93982/selection/d329eb2cfe1e45b202a882b919adbe3a30dcd36b8ae052be410fce81fb55ae78"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-93982" :question/id #uuid "95bc1c5a-4cad-5587-8969-cf8149e63588" :question/math-academy-id "q-93982" :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix $A$ above. Which of the following represents the corresponding bilinear form ${x}^{T}\\,Ay$ in terms of the components of $x=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]$ and $y=[\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{aligned}]?$" :question/worked-solution "**Method 1**\n\nEach entry ${a}_{ij}$ of $A$ corresponds to the term ${a}_{ij}{x}_{i}{y}_{j}$ in the expression of the bilinear form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{T}\\,Ay & =3{x}_{1}{y}_{1}+1{x}_{1}{y}_{2}+(-1){x}_{2}{y}_{1}+2{x}_{2}{y}_{2} \\\\  & =3{x}_{1}{y}_{1}+{x}_{1}{y}_{2}-{x}_{2}{y}_{1}+2{x}_{2}{y}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nTo write down a bilinear form in terms of vector components, we compute the following expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{T}\\,Ay & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3{y}_{1}+{y}_{2} \\\\ -{y}_{1}+2{y}_{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={x}_{1}(3{y}_{1}+{y}_{2})+{x}_{2}(-{y}_{1}+2{y}_{2}) \\\\  & =3{x}_{1}{y}_{1}+{x}_{1}{y}_{2}-{x}_{2}{y}_{1}+2{x}_{2}{y}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-93982/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "55277d69-eedc-5c5c-883a-083746e00947"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-93982"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-94004"] :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ -3 & -4\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix $A$ above. Which of the following represents the corresponding bilinear form ${x}^{T}\\,Ay$ in terms of the components of $x=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]$ and $y=[\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{aligned}]?$" :question/worked-solution "**Method 1**\n\nEach entry ${a}_{ij}$ of $A$ corresponds to the term ${a}_{ij}{x}_{i}{y}_{j}$ in the expression of the bilinear form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{T}\\,Ay & =(3){x}_{1}{y}_{1}+2{x}_{1}{y}_{2}+(-3){x}_{2}{y}_{1}+-4{x}_{2}{y}_{2} \\\\  & =3{x}_{1}{y}_{1}+2{x}_{1}{y}_{2}-3{x}_{2}{y}_{1}-4{x}_{2}{y}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nTo write down a bilinear form in terms of vector components, we compute the following expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{T}\\,Ay & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ -3 & -4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3{y}_{1}+2{y}_{2} \\\\ -3{y}_{1}-4{y}_{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={x}_{1}(3{y}_{1}+2{y}_{2})+{x}_{2}(-3{y}_{1}-4{y}_{2}) \\\\  & =3{x}_{1}{y}_{1}+2{x}_{1}{y}_{2}-3{x}_{2}{y}_{1}-4{x}_{2}{y}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-94057/selection/ae9425c9e204310ed598f729a242e0b42a2acbbf125bff30bc2080e10b8cf473" :answer/id #uuid "b5a81527-9cbf-533b-b0dd-a58842ffdc28" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94057/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "8c40c08b-c93d-5def-af01-c24b25ae8939" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94057/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer/id #uuid "a1cfac5e-9efd-554c-a559-1e0f5d0b8357" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94057/selection/7f2aea1619f9c4cbe5384e0826442d82ebdb1ac614452244ced54b63c0c77efe" :answer/id #uuid "716c2ae5-3dd7-564a-9933-303c6c2e55cb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94057/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" :answer/id #uuid "a2f13e28-1f68-58cc-83fb-910473ea581a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94057/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "ed45c267-15d0-55f9-8584-ff5e403bcc8e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-94057/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" :answer-field/choices ["q-94057/selection/ae9425c9e204310ed598f729a242e0b42a2acbbf125bff30bc2080e10b8cf473" "q-94057/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" "q-94057/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" "q-94057/selection/7f2aea1619f9c4cbe5384e0826442d82ebdb1ac614452244ced54b63c0c77efe" "q-94057/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-94057" :question/id #uuid "b10e7084-45ad-5978-87c8-4808b0be70b8" :question/math-academy-id "q-94057" :question/problem "$$\n[\\begin{aligned}0 & a & 0 \\\\ b & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -3 & c\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe matrix of the bilinear form $B(x,y)={x}_{1}{y}_{2}+3{x}_{2}{y}_{1}-3{x}_{3}{y}_{2}+2{x}_{3}{y}_{3}$ is given above. What is the value of $a+b+c?$" :question/worked-solution "Each term ${a}_{ij}{x}_{i}{y}_{j}$ in the expression of the bilinear form corresponds to the entry ${a}_{ij}$ of the matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B(x,y) & ={x}_{1}{y}_{2}+3{x}_{2}{y}_{1}-3{x}_{3}{y}_{2}+2{x}_{3}{y}_{3} \\\\  & =0{x}_{1}{y}_{1}+1{x}_{1}{y}_{2}+0{x}_{1}{y}_{3} \\\\  & +\\,3{x}_{2}{y}_{1}+0{x}_{2}{y}_{2}+0{x}_{2}{y}_{3} \\\\  & +\\,0{x}_{3}{y}_{1}+(-3){x}_{3}{y}_{2}+2{x}_{3}{y}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, the corresponding matrix of the bilinear form is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=1,$ $b=3,$ and $c=2.$ Finally, \n\n$$\na+b+c=1+3+2=6.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-94057/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f60cd05d-e4af-5bf1-8827-cab48da934f1"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-94057"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-140853/selection/478cbf1ea235fbfb5b60a0837fffa0a678f83a3bcb8f958a024b0760ea2175ce" :answer/id #uuid "b2ebb4f8-da81-590f-b864-dcd9284598cd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "11" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140853/selection/801bcdd9cb6a10cec998162e05f71050c8aaf0c6974f095bdcaef715a09f4aee" :answer/id #uuid "3fc25b48-e112-5f68-8e77-6f57099aeb50" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "21" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140853/selection/a20b3c9808c291c56ec5bfc5f0f93a856fc692714ca7ebd36c5e4bc361f7075c" :answer/id #uuid "55ae36c2-2d7f-533c-ba1f-473ff3462994" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "42" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140853/selection/650efaaa01beaa7de6c030497edff1dd29c570bf683f3726bbcacabc3dfa7e4c" :answer/id #uuid "ba0f3095-cf7b-5d71-9a79-e3b700e224d2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "16" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140853/selection/e326a281f601aec64d5dcce4921033c5f93cbf7f8b0a7a5809a9962dfadde666" :answer/id #uuid "aa86bd07-88ac-5bdb-8039-5173c1cc21c5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "18" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140853/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "5aa60481-686a-5eb6-ac2e-42effa99d225" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-140853/selection/801bcdd9cb6a10cec998162e05f71050c8aaf0c6974f095bdcaef715a09f4aee" :answer-field/choices ["q-140853/selection/478cbf1ea235fbfb5b60a0837fffa0a678f83a3bcb8f958a024b0760ea2175ce" "q-140853/selection/801bcdd9cb6a10cec998162e05f71050c8aaf0c6974f095bdcaef715a09f4aee" "q-140853/selection/a20b3c9808c291c56ec5bfc5f0f93a856fc692714ca7ebd36c5e4bc361f7075c" "q-140853/selection/650efaaa01beaa7de6c030497edff1dd29c570bf683f3726bbcacabc3dfa7e4c" "q-140853/selection/e326a281f601aec64d5dcce4921033c5f93cbf7f8b0a7a5809a9962dfadde666"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-140853" :question/id #uuid "ac50817d-d0cd-5bab-aa46-bd534774fa22" :question/math-academy-id "q-140853" :question/problem "Consider the bilinear form $B(x,y),$ given by \n\n$$\nB(x,y)=2{x}_{1}{y}_{2}+{x}_{1}{y}_{3}-3{x}_{2}{y}_{2}+2{x}_{3}{y}_{1}.\n$$\n\n \n\nEvaluate $B(x,y)$ when $x=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]$ and $y=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "We are given that \n\n$\\,$ $x=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]\\,$ and $\\,y=[\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{3}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$\n\nSubstituting these into the bilinear expression, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B(x,y) & =2{x}_{1}{y}_{2}+{x}_{1}{y}_{3}-3{x}_{2}{y}_{2}+2{x}_{3}{y}_{1} \\\\  & =2\\cdot 3\\cdot 5+3\\cdot 2-3\\cdot 1\\cdot 5+2\\cdot (-2)\\cdot 0 \\\\  & =30+6-15+0 \\\\  & =21.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-140853/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7083d465-9871-59ca-97fa-583e740e961f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-140853"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
